ext request. But the first request can't wait for a reply.\n\nLet me think about this differently. In a propagator network:\n\n- user-ingress is a cell that gets new values (user messages)\n- I need a behavior:source that accumulates user messages\n- I need a behavior:source that accumulates assistant replies\n- I need to combine them into conversation history\n- When a new user message arrives, trigger a model request\n- The model request includes the history\n- The model's response is executable Lain that calls the reply function\n- The reply function delivers and adds to history\n\nFor the \"no cycle\" constraint: the first request should only include the current user message (no prior replies). Subsequent requests include prior messages.\n\nLet me think about how to structure this:\n\n```\n;; Temporal sources for user and assistant messages\n(define conv:user-source (behavior:source))\n(define conv:assistant-source (behavior:source))\n\n;; Connect user-ingress to user source\n;; But how? user-ingress is a cell...\n```\n\nHmm, I think I need to use a different approach. Let me look at the construction-review-cell warning: \"each call to behavior:source creates a DISTINCT source, so writing to another unnamed instance does not feed a previously created scan.\"\n\nAnd: \"A bare acknowledged record must be converted to a temporal occurrence before feeding a temporal source.\"\n\nI think the pattern for user-ingress is:\n- user-ingress is a cell\n- I connect it to a behavior:source: `(-> user-ingress conv:user-source)`\n- Each new value from user-ingress becomes an occurrence in conv:user-source\n\nBut the warning says \"Temporal sources accept occurrences from event:point, never bare message records.\" Does this mean I can't connect a cell directly", :finish-reason "stop", :truncated? false, :response-sequence 2, :request-id "construction"}, :inputs #{#propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "02a8526f-970a-32ab-bfc1-b9611c2cc366"} #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "01a